{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/960945-abomination-npcs","id":960945,"title":"Abomination NPCs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-31T01:50:55-07:00","id":960945,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Abomination NPCs","content":"So Abominations don't hold any interest to me as player characters because well they are foresaken Abominations in perpetual Harano that quickly circle the drain. But as an NPC they do have potential. The line in the players guide that if they relinquish themselves to the Wyrm they halt gnosis drain and become true wyrmish monsters. This sounds to me like the perfect story arch about preventing the rise of a Wyrmish beast that could kickstart the apocalypse. The Pack hopping across the country/world to stop a cult from raising the abomination from Torpor. The Abomination itself could have been some great hero of one of the Tribes, hell why not an actual prefall White Howler! But it was one of the damned unlucky Garou who actually were embraced rather then dying in the process. Eventually it falls to the Wyrm when it can't end its own life and is driven from the People.<br /> <br /> One of my ideas for a Kickstarter for the Apocalypse was the Four Horsemen each Representing one of the Heads of the Wyrm, with Death the Fourth Horseman tied to Apep as the Head/Anus of the Wyrm tied to oblivion. The Horseman of Famine tied to the Eater of Souls would be a Garou Abomination. In case you were wondering my own take on the first Ronin essentially looked like the Beast from Angel, as its homid form, with each form a unique mutation like Nightmasters Boss forms.<br /> <br /> But it would be an interesting type of NPC if arisen, similar to say a Baali with that level 9 Daimonion power that lets its master possess it, hell that could be the actual goal where the Abomination tries to achieve Daimonion level 9 to manifest a Maeljin or even an aspect of the Wyrm and fully bring about the Apocalypse. But a Homid Ahroun (Whatever tribe lets say Shadowlord or White Howler) of 4th or 5th rank falling to the Wyrm is already a scary foe, but if the fall was becoming an Abomination is a pretty neat grab bag of Tricks using disciplines, and then possession by spirits further makes it rather out there.<br /> <br /> But hey to me this reads as an actual kosher way to do a cool NPC crossover. Give it Daimonion and Obtenebration and woof thats scary, then toss in Fomori mutations and you can essentially make up whatever neat trick you want to through at a group.<br /> <br /> Come on you know you love it. &gt;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T01:55:46-07:00","id":960947,"title":"","content":"Also worth noting I use the houserule that Abominations step sideways into the Shadowlands rather then the Penumbra. It just feels so damn appropriate, and I love any reason to get a pack into the Underworld. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What houserules do you apply to Abominations, or even Garou Wraiths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T06:37:11-07:00","id":961015,"title":"","content":"There are no Garou Wraiths in my games (with the rare exceptions from the Silent Striders). Garou have three fates in my games when they die. If they have a permanent Willpower below 5, their spirits dissolve and join with the Penumbra. If they have a permanent Willpower of 5 or higher but a Rank below 5, they reincarnate into the next generation of Garou or Kinfolk, depending on the need for souls If they have a permanent Willpower 5 or higher and a Rank 5 or hogher, they become ancestor spirits for their tribe. Kinfolk with a Willpower 5 or higher may be reincarnated as Kinfolk or Garou, depending on the need for the need for souls. Humans or wolves of great virtue may be reincarnated as Garou or Kinfolk as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T06:41:13-07:00","id":961016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination\"> NPC Question: (BSD?) Abomination - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I know ALL the reasons not to allow such a beast in a game. WW and various purists can be quoted all over the place. I'm not here for that. I'm here to get some help and input into making such a Beast viable as an NPC who will start as an Ally, become a Mentor, and eventually be revealed as a terrible Enemy. All over centuries. So, I need suggestions on making a character that CAN last the centuries. Not a Harano-crushed soul who greets the sun. Not a raving psycho who commits suicide by Wyrm/Vampire/Garou Pack/etc. Perhaps he'll go through these stages...I can't really say at this point. But, let's </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}